From 66732e72b1123af3963f7bddbf5b0a9eb49e1dbf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:50:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): CLI and dashboard dispatch honour the
 core-update drain hold [daveey]

`dispatch_once` checked only the gateway's own draining snapshot; only the gateway watcher read
hermes-sync's core-update drain hold (`agent.core_update_drain`). So `hermes kanban dispatch` and the
dashboard `POST /dispatch` (both call `dispatch_once` directly) could claim and spawn inside a hold.

Problem: hermes-hub 2026-11-11 02:10:36Z, `hermes kanban dispatch --json` (pid 4128172) claimed
t_01a1c7dcfabfb0f1 run 165540 (lock hermes-hub:4128172) inside drainer 4107500's claim-hold
[02:08:42, 02:18:43]; the gateway logged dispatch-held at 02:08:44 and claimed nothing.
Why 1: the claim came from the CLI process, not the gateway (lock pid = CLI pid) -- the "PID discrepancy"
  in the Path P evidence is this.
Why 2: `_cmd_dispatch` -> `dispatch_once` has no drain-hold check; it only reads `dispatch_paused()`
  (gateway_state draining) -- hermes_cli/kanban_db_dispatch.py, kanban_gateway_drain.py.
Why 3: the hold was enforced at the caller (gateway/kanban_watchers_common.py `_kanban_dispatch_gate`)
  instead of in the shared tick, while core_update_drain.py promises "the kanban dispatcher spawns nothing".
Root (happened): a safety gate placed in one caller of a shared entry point instead of the entry point.
Root (not caught): drain-hold tests drove only the gateway watcher; no test exercised the other
  `dispatch_once` callers under a hold.
Recurrence: first time for this path (gateway-side drain cards t_d97d2b17 et al. covered the watcher).

Fix: `dispatch_once` reads the live hold after bookkeeping/placement (reclaim, wake probes, promotion
still run, as in the gateway's held tick) and returns before the spawn budget, recording the hold on
`DispatchResult.core_update_drain_hold`; `claim_if_admitting` rechecks it at claim time (both lanes) so a
hold that starts mid-tick still refuses. Dead-writer holds don't count (`read_hold`), and a missing
module fails open, both as in the gateway gate. CLI JSON/text report the hold as the reason for 0
spawned. Caps (max_spawn / max_in_progress / memory pressure) are untouched.

Proof: tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_dispatch_core_drain_hold.py 13/13 RED on origin/main, 13/13 GREEN
(CLI + dashboard x ready + review under live hold; dead-pid hold claims; mid-tick hold; fail-open;
promotion kept; CLI text). Mutants of each added condition (tick check, claim recheck, ImportError,
JSON field, text) each killed. 33 affected dispatch/drain/dashboard/cron-hold files: 360 passed, 0 failed.
`scripts/check --base origin/main` ok; FILE_LINES offset by moving `_call_spawn_fn` to
kanban_db_dispatch_spawn_call.py (re-imported under the old name), CC offset by `_print_zero_spawn_reasons`.
